    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d450">

                <pb facs="0459" n="369" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg369"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/2652</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Irkutsk</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Harris</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d450-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Irkutsk</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-09-07"><hi rendition="#italic">September 7</hi> (<hi
                                rendition="#italic">6?</hi>), <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >1918</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received September 9,
                            4.15 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Telegraphic communication again reestablished with Ekaterinburg and Samara. No
                    material change in the situation on that front as Czechs are carrying on
                    defensive warfare until reenforcements arrive. Two thousand two hundred Czechs
                    and Siberians from here were sent westward last week. An attempt will be made
                    shortly to capture Perm.</p>
                <closer>[<signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Harris</hi></signed>]</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d450-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d450-f1-content">
                <p>Sent via the Legation in China.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
